<title>BRAZIL: Strike at Daimler-Benz Brazil halts output.</title>
<headline>Strike at Daimler-Benz Brazil halts output.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Production at Daimler-Benz AG Brazil truck plant was halted due to a second-day strike of hundreds of workers demanding a profit sharing policy and cut in daily working hours, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>Mercedes-Benz truck plant makes 140 trucks and bus chassis a day, he said.</p>
<p>Nearly 4,000 workers at the production line entered on strike Monday and they will hold a meeting later today to decide if they will go on with the strike, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
</text>
